# trivy ignore — CVEs we have triaged and accepted.
#
# Only test-only transitive dependencies belong here. Runtime deps must be
# fixed by version bump, never silenced. Each entry must record:
#   - the CVE id,
#   - the package it was reported against,
#   - the rationale (test-only path / not linked into prod binary),
#   - and ideally the upstream fix tracker.
#
# Re-audit on every dockertest bump. If any of these flips into a runtime
# path, remove the suppression and bump.

# --- services/indexer-go test deps (ory/dockertest/v3 chain) ---------------
#
# dockertest spins up Postgres in a container for the migration apply/rollback
# integration test. It pulls docker/cli, docker/docker, and runc transitively.
# These libraries are imported only by *_integration_test.go (build tag
# `integration`) and never linked into the indexer-go binary — so a CVE in
# their daemon-side code path is not exploitable in our deployed image.

# docker/docker — Moby project. Transitive via dockertest.
CVE-2026-34040  # daemon-only path, test-only dep; tracking dockertest upgrade
CVE-2024-41110  # AuthZ plugin bypass, daemon-only; test-only dep

# docker/cli — CLI scanner. Transitive via dockertest.
CVE-2025-15558  # CLI-only, test-only dep

# opencontainers/runc — container runtime. Transitive via dockertest.
CVE-2025-52881  # runtime-only, test-only dep
CVE-2025-52565  # runtime-only, test-only dep
CVE-2025-31133  # runtime-only, test-only dep
CVE-2024-21626  # leaked fd, runtime-only; test-only dep
